{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774714,"nonce":"/fvJDQN+/jyFx1h2al3CnzXZg6g=","title":"fix(forge/github): checkout credential requests contents:read, never write","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #23 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/clone-credential-contents-read` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-17T17:26:12Z · Merged: 2026-07-17T17:40:40Z\n\n`mint_checkout_credential` requested `contents: write` for non-fork runs. A checkout only **reads** the tree (ADR-0045; `scarab-clone.sh` only fetches/checks-out/pulls-LFS), so write is never needed — and it **422s** on any installation granted only `contents: read` (`\"The level of access for permissions requested are not granted to this installation.\"`), silently falling back to an **anonymous** clone. That masks a broken minted-token path on public repos and fully breaks it on private ones (git-bug `1b5d5c7`).\n\nAlways request `contents: read`. `read_only` still governs the fork-PR lockdown of the returned `CheckoutCredential`, not the token scope.\n\nVerified: `cargo test -p scarab-forge-github` green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}